.TH HALCYON-MODEM 1 "November 2026" "halcyon 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-modem \- encode and decode Halcyon frames
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-modem
.B selftest
.br
.B halcyon-modem
.B rungs
.br
.B halcyon-modem
.B tx
\fB\-\-mcs\fR \fIN\fR \fB\-\-text\fR \fISTRING\fR \fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR
.br
.B halcyon-modem
.B rx
\fB\-\-in\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-repeat\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halcyon-modem
is the C++17 implementation of the Halcyon modem core.  It reads and writes
raw little-endian float32 baseband at 12 kHz, the same format the Python
implementation uses, and it is wire-compatible with it in both directions.
.PP
The wide profile is supported: all 17 speed levels, from QPSK 1/2 to 256QAM
8/9.  The narrower robust and compact geometries and the single-tone 16-FSK
path exist only in the Python modem.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B selftest
Transmit and receive every supported speed level back to back and report
which ones pass.
.TP
.B rungs
Print the speed ladder: level, modulation, code rate, bit rate and occupied
bandwidth.
.TP
.B tx
Encode a frame at speed level \fIN\fR and write the baseband samples to
\fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B rx
Acquire and decode one burst from \fIFILE\fR and print a JSON result.  With
\fB\-\-repeat\fR \fIN\fR, decode it \fIN\fR times and report the mean
milliseconds per frame.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-data " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the rate tables from \fIPATH\fR instead of the default.  Without this
option halcyon-modem looks beside its own binary, then in
\fI/usr/share/halcyon/wide.bin\fR, then in \fIcpp/data/wide.bin\fR relative
to the working directory.  The Debian package installs the table it needs, so
this is only useful for a build tree or a copy of the tables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HALCYON_DEBUG
When set to 1, print acquisition, header and payload diagnostics on stderr.
.TP
.B HALCYON_DATA
Path to the rate-table file, equivalent to \fB\-\-data\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B halcyon-modem selftest
.TP
.B halcyon-modem tx --mcs 4 --text "test de halcyon k" --out frame.f32
.TP
.B halcyon-modem rx --in frame.f32
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR halcyon (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Halcyon authors.
